---
description: Every testable UI element needs a stable data-testid (module-field-type)
globs: src/**/*.{js,jsx}
alwaysApply: false
---

# data-testid on every testable element

Any new or edited input, textarea, button, link, dropdown trigger / option / selected value,
error or success message, table row, row action button, modal or toast must have a `data-testid`.
Do not add it to plain wrapper divs. Never change an existing `data-testid`.

Pattern: `module-field-type`, lowercase, hyphen-separated — e.g. `employee-emp-id-input`,
`employee-gender-select`, `employee-gender-option-male`, `employee-email-error`, `employee-save-button`.

- Values are fixed and readable: never random, never from state or list index.
- Database options use the option text or id: `employee-department-option-it-team`.
- Table rows use the record's business id: `employee-row-lc005`; actions in a row:
  `employee-row-lc005-edit-button`.

Helpers in `src/shared/testing/testId.jsx`: `testId(...parts)`, `rowTestId(module, record, ...parts)`,
`itemTestKey(item)` (business key of a list item: emp_id / code / name / label / value / id),
`<TestIdModule name="...">`, `useTestIdModule()`.

Inside `.map()` build the id from the item, never the index:
`testId("pay-type-frequency", v, "button")`, `testId("sidebar-menu", itemTestKey(item), "link")`.
In HTML strings (Swal `html:`) write the attribute directly: `data-testid="${testId(module, "reset-password", label, "input")}"`.

Shared components already emit ids — set the module, don't hand-write them:
- `FormTextField` / `FormAutocomplete` / `FormDatePicker` / `FormTimePicker` / `FormSwitch` /
  `FormCheckbox` / `FormToggleGroup` → `<module>-<name>-input|select|switch|checkbox|option-*|error`
  (pass `testId` to override the `<module>-<name>` base).
- `SidebarFormLayout` / `FormDrawer` (`testIdModule` prop) → `-form`, `-save-button`, `-cancel-button`.
- `AppTable` (`testIdModule`, `getRowTestId`) → `-table`, `-search-input`, `-row-<id>`.
- `useConfirm(module)`, `Swal.fire({ testId })`, and all `toast.*` (`toast-success-message`) are covered.
- react-select (`shared/ui/TestableSelect`), `DateTimePicker`, `PropertySelect`, `EditCell`, `LocationTag`,
  payroll `Switch` take a `testId` base prop → `-trigger|select`, `-option-<text>`, `-clear-button`, …
- reactstrap `ModalHeader` close button: `close={<ModalCloseButton onClick={toggle} testId="x-close-button" />}`.
- Sidebar forms opened through `DisplayForms` get their module from `src/shared/testing/testIdModules.js`;
  add new component names there.

```jsx
// ❌
<Button onClick={save}>Save</Button>
<button onClick={() => remove(row.original)}>…</button>
// ✅
<Button onClick={save} data-testid="holiday-save-button">Save</Button>
<IconButton data-testid={rowTestId("holiday", row.original, "delete-button")} …>
```
